{#
  Sub-navigation for « Supervision » — three screens, one menu entry: the
  menu names the function, these tabs name the screens it contains.

  The component is the shared `partials/page_picker.html.twig`, as in
  finance, fees, rental and groups: the pages[] → nav rail layer, written
  once (design.md §7.6). This module first shipped its own `nav-pills`
  row, which gave the site's sub-navigation a third visual style —
  exactly what the page_picker exists to prevent.

  `match_prefix`: a detail page belongs to the tab it is opened from.
  /support-dashboard/tickets/12 selects « Tickets », and the longest
  prefix wins, so never « Tableau de bord » as well.

  (Translated from French on the change that added the third screen —
  AGENTS.md § Language: a Twig comment is a comment, so it is English.)
#}
{% include 'partials/page_picker.html.twig' with {
    picker_id: 'support-dashboard-page-picker',
    pages: [
        {'url': '/support-dashboard', 'label': 'Tableau de bord'},
        {'url': '/support-dashboard/tickets', 'label': 'Tickets'},
        {'url': '/support-dashboard/correspondances', 'label': 'Correspondances'},
    ],
    current_path: current_path,
    match_prefix: true,
    aria_label: 'Pages Supervision',
} only %}
